# Bendy and the Dark Revival (PPSA27624): reach Chapter 1 gameplay.
#
# Anchors are SECONDS from the first pad poll (pad.cpp:207-210 -- a bare number is seconds,
# 'f' is flips, 'p' is pad reads). Observed on a bounded screenshot run, 2026-08-20:
#
#   t~0-20   opening movie (the 15,168 ms source; #1981's media clock ends it)
#   t~50-65  title screen with BEGIN; draws_last climbs 2 -> 3 -> 7 -> 12
#   t~70     Media/level2 (Core/2_General/Game) + Media/level4
#            (Core/3_Sections/Section_S101_JoeyDrewApartment) open together; draws_last 23
#   t~87     draws_last 1014 -- the section is rendering
#   t~118    Media/level5 + Media/level6 (Section_S102_ArchGateOffices,
#            Section_S103_JoeyDrewExhibit)
#
# Cross alone carries the whole menu path and skips the opening cutscenes (their SKIP prompt is
# bound to Cross). The first in-world interaction prompt is 'STAND' bound to SQUARE and is a
# HOLD, so Square is held 2 s at a time. Square is kept out of the first 120 s so it can never
# land on the save-slot screen, whose Square binding this route has not established.
#
# THE ROUTE IS SAVE-STATE DEPENDENT. Run it with a FRESH PROSPER_SAVE0 directory. With a save
# already present the same button sequence takes the CONTINUE path off the save-slot screen instead
# of NEW GAME: measured 2026-08-20, a clean run opened level4 then level5+level6, while an immediate
# rerun against the previous run's save opened level5+level6 with NO level4, ran at draws_last ~200
# instead of ~1000-1200, and printed 'Game Loaded.'. Both reach gameplay, so this is a determinism
# requirement and not a failure -- but a route validated without it is measuring two different things
# on alternate runs. PROSPER_SAVE0 is read at prosper/src/hle/fs/hle_file.cpp:486; it must also be
# per-title, because save data is not namespaced by title (#2734) and the default
# /tmp/prosper-savedata0 is shared with every other game.
#
# Progress oracle is the Unity scene index, not pixels: Media/levelNN is the build-settings
# scene index (37 scene paths in Media/globalgamemanagers against 37 Media/levelNN files).
# level2 = Core/2_General/Game is the persistent menu/game scene and is reached at the title
# screen, so it is NOT a gameplay signal; any levelN with N >= 4 is a Section_S1xx_* scene.
